---
// Unlisted page: not linked from anywhere in the site and marked noindex,
// so it's reachable only by direct link. Served at /sisteradventure
// Fully self-contained on purpose, so it doesn't inherit the site nav/layout.
// Interactive bits (lodging pop-ups, packing checklist, countdown) are plain
// vanilla JS in the is:inline script at the bottom. Checklist saves to this
// browser's localStorage under the key 'tmb-packing-v1'.
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
<title>Evan &amp; Erin · Tour du Mont Blanc</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wght@12..96,500;12..96,600;12..96,700&family=Newsreader:ital,opsz,wght@0,6..72,400;0,6..72,500;1,6..72,400&family=Space+Mono:wght@400;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style is:global>
  :root{
    --paper:#E9EBE6;
    --card:#F3F4F0;
    --ink:#1E2D27;
    --spruce:#2C4339;
    --glacier:#5E8497;
    --signal:#AE463C;
    --stone:#777C72;
    --line:#CCD1C9;
  }
  *{box-sizing:border-box;}
  html{-webkit-text-size-adjust:100%;}
  body{
    margin:0;
    background:var(--paper);
    color:var(--ink);
    font-family:"Newsreader",Georgia,serif;
    font-size:17px;
    line-height:1.5;
    -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;
  }
  .wrap{max-width:880px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 28px 72px;}

  /* ---- data/mono token ---- */
  .mono{font-family:"Space Mono",ui-monospace,monospace;}
  .eyebrow{
    font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;
    font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:.22em;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--glacier);
  }

  /* ---- header ---- */
  header{position:relative;overflow:hidden;padding:64px 28px 40px;margin:0 -28px;}
  .contour{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;z-index:0;color:var(--spruce);opacity:.10;}
  .contour svg{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;}
  header > *{position:relative;z-index:1;}
  h1{
    font-family:"Bricolage Grotesque",sans-serif;
    font-weight:700;
    font-size:clamp(40px,8.5vw,76px);
    line-height:.95;
    letter-spacing:-.02em;
    margin:14px 0 0;
    color:var(--spruce);
  }
  h1 .small{display:block;font-size:.42em;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:var(--ink);margin-top:.35em;}
  .lede{
    margin:18px 0 0;max-width:46ch;color:var(--ink);font-size:18px;
  }
  .lede em{color:var(--stone);font-style:italic;}

  /* ---- stat strip ---- */
  .stats{
    display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:30px;margin-top:30px;
    padding-top:22px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .stat .n{font-family:"Bricolage Grotesque",sans-serif;font-weight:600;font-size:26px;color:var(--spruce);line-height:1;}
  .stat .l{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--stone);margin-top:7px;}

  /* ---- country ribbon ---- */
  .ribbon{display:flex;margin:26px 0 4px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:2px;overflow:hidden;}
  .leg{flex:1;padding:9px 12px;font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.1em;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;color:#fff;}
  .leg small{opacity:.8;font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.08em;}
  .leg.fr{background:var(--spruce);flex:2.1;}
  .leg.it{background:var(--glacier);flex:2.4;}
  .leg.ch{background:#4a6b5c;flex:3.1;}
  .leg.fr2{background:var(--spruce);flex:1.1;}

  /* ---- section heading ---- */
  .sec{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--signal);margin:54px 0 4px;}
  .sec-rule{height:1px;background:var(--line);margin-bottom:18px;}

  /* ---- trail spine ---- */
  .trail{position:relative;margin-top:8px;}
  .day{position:relative;display:grid;grid-template-columns:54px 1fr;column-gap:20px;padding:0 0 26px;}
  .spinecol{position:relative;}
  .spinecol::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:18px;top:6px;bottom:-26px;width:2px;background:var(--line);}
  .day:last-of-type .spinecol::before{display:none;}
  .node{
    position:relative;z-index:1;width:38px;height:38px;border-radius:50%;
    background:var(--spruce);color:var(--paper);
    display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
    font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-weight:700;font-size:14px;
  }
  .node.rest{background:var(--paper);border:2px dashed var(--glacier);color:var(--glacier);font-size:8.5px;letter-spacing:.05em;}

  .content{padding-top:1px;}
  .date{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--stone);}
  .route{font-size:20px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.25;margin:3px 0 0;color:var(--ink);}
  .route .via{color:var(--stone);font-style:italic;font-weight:400;font-size:.82em;}
  .row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline;gap:6px 16px;margin-top:7px;}
  .stay{font-size:15px;}
  .stay b{font-weight:500;}
  .stay .tag{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--glacier);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:2px;padding:1px 6px;margin-left:2px;vertical-align:1px;}
  .metrics{margin-left:auto;display:flex;gap:13px;align-items:baseline;font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;white-space:nowrap;}
  .dist{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:12px;color:var(--spruce);white-space:nowrap;}
  .up{font-size:12px;color:var(--glacier);}
  .note{font-size:14.5px;color:var(--stone);margin:8px 0 0;max-width:62ch;}
  .prox{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--glacier);margin:8px 0 0;display:flex;gap:7px;align-items:baseline;}
  .prox::before{content:"";flex:0 0 auto;width:6px;height:6px;margin-top:4px;border:1.5px solid var(--glacier);border-radius:50%;}
  .day.restday .route{color:var(--glacier);}

  /* elevation infographic */
  .chartwrap{margin-top:10px;overflow-x:auto;}
  .chart{width:100%;min-width:620px;height:auto;display:block;}
  .chart .bar{fill:var(--spruce);stroke:var(--paper);stroke-width:1.2;}
  .chart .cap{stroke:var(--glacier);stroke-width:2.5;}
  .chart .grid{stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:1;stroke-dasharray:2 5;}
  .chart .axis{stroke:var(--stone);stroke-width:1.2;}
  .chart .rest{stroke:var(--glacier);stroke-width:1;stroke-dasharray:2 3;}
  .chart text{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;}
  .chart .glabel{fill:var(--spruce);font-size:9.5px;}
  .chart .dnum{fill:var(--spruce);font-size:11px;font-weight:700;}
  .chart .dmi{fill:var(--stone);font-size:8.5px;}
  .chart .ylab{fill:var(--stone);font-size:9px;}
  .chart .restlab{fill:var(--glacier);font-size:8px;letter-spacing:.14em;}
  .chartcap{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.04em;color:var(--stone);margin:14px 0 0;line-height:1.65;}
  .chartcap b{color:var(--spruce);font-weight:700;}

  /* border crossing marker */
  .cross{display:grid;grid-template-columns:54px 1fr;column-gap:20px;padding:0 0 26px;}
  .cross .spinecol{position:relative;}
  .cross .spinecol::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:18px;top:-6px;bottom:-26px;width:2px;background:var(--line);}
  .cross .pin{position:relative;z-index:1;width:14px;height:14px;margin:8px 0 0 12px;background:var(--signal);transform:rotate(45deg);border-radius:2px;}
  .cross .label{padding-top:4px;font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--signal);}
  .cross .label small{display:block;color:var(--stone);letter-spacing:.06em;margin-top:2px;}

  /* ---- booking tiers ---- */
  .tier{background:var(--card);border-left:3px solid var(--line);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0;padding:16px 20px;margin-bottom:14px;}
  .tier.t1{border-left-color:var(--signal);}
  .tier.t2{border-left-color:var(--glacier);}
  .tier.t3{border-left-color:var(--spruce);}
  .tier h3{font-family:"Bricolage Grotesque",sans-serif;font-weight:600;font-size:16px;margin:0;color:var(--ink);}
  .tier .when{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--stone);margin:3px 0 10px;}
  .tier ul{margin:0;padding:0;list-style:none;}
  .tier li{font-size:15px;padding:3px 0;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:14px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);}
  .tier li:first-child{border-top:0;}
  .tier li .d{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:11px;color:var(--glacier);white-space:nowrap;}

  /* ---- notes ---- */
  .notes{columns:2;column-gap:36px;margin-top:6px;}
  .notes p{break-inside:avoid;margin:0 0 14px;font-size:15px;color:var(--ink);}
  .notes p b{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--signal);display:block;margin-bottom:2px;font-weight:700;}

  footer{margin-top:50px;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.05em;color:var(--stone);display:flex;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;}

  @media (max-width:640px){
    body{font-size:16px;}
    .notes{columns:1;}
    .metrics{margin-left:0;}
    .day,.cross{column-gap:14px;grid-template-columns:44px 1fr;}
    .spinecol::before,.cross .spinecol::before{left:15px;}
    .node{width:32px;height:32px;font-size:12px;}
    .cross .pin{margin-left:9px;}
  }

  /* interactive lodging */
  .hint{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.05em;color:var(--stone);margin:-8px 0 18px;}
  .lodge{font:inherit;font-weight:500;color:var(--ink);background:none;border:none;padding:0 0 1px;cursor:pointer;border-bottom:1.5px dotted var(--glacier);transition:color .12s;}
  .lodge:hover{color:var(--glacier);}
  dialog#lodgeModal{border:none;border-radius:5px;padding:0;max-width:520px;width:calc(100% - 40px);background:var(--card);color:var(--ink);box-shadow:0 24px 60px rgba(30,45,39,.35);}
  dialog#lodgeModal::backdrop{background:rgba(30,45,39,.55);}
  .modal-art svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;}
  .modal-body{padding:18px 24px 22px;}
  .modal-body h3{font-family:"Bricolage Grotesque",sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:23px;margin:0;color:var(--spruce);}
  .modal-sub{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--glacier);margin:4px 0 12px;}
  .modal-kv{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:4px 16px;font-size:14.5px;margin:0 0 12px;}
  .modal-kv dt{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--stone);padding-top:2px;}
  .modal-kv dd{margin:0;}
  .modal-blurb{font-size:15px;margin:0 0 6px;}
  .modal-book{font-size:13.5px;color:var(--stone);margin:0 0 16px;}
  .modal-actions{display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:center;}
  .modal-actions a{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.05em;color:var(--paper);background:var(--spruce);text-decoration:none;padding:9px 14px;border-radius:3px;}
  .modal-actions a:hover{background:var(--glacier);}
  .modal-actions button{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:12px;color:var(--stone);background:none;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:3px;padding:8px 14px;cursor:pointer;}
  /* packing checklist */
  .packgrid{columns:2;column-gap:36px;}
  .pack{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;break-inside:avoid;padding:4px 0;font-size:15px;cursor:pointer;}
  .pack input{accent-color:var(--spruce);transform:translateY(1px);}
  .pack.done span{color:var(--stone);text-decoration:line-through;text-decoration-color:var(--glacier);}
  .packadd{display:flex;gap:8px;margin-top:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;}
  .packadd input{font-family:"Newsreader",serif;font-size:15px;padding:7px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:3px;background:var(--card);color:var(--ink);flex:1;min-width:180px;}
  .packadd button{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:.05em;padding:7px 14px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:3px;background:var(--card);color:var(--spruce);cursor:pointer;}
  .packadd button:hover{border-color:var(--glacier);color:var(--glacier);}
  /* phrasebook */
  .phrases{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14.5px;}
  .phrases th{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--glacier);text-align:left;padding:6px 10px 6px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);}
  .phrases td{padding:7px 10px 7px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top;}
  .phrases td:first-child{color:var(--stone);}
  .phrases em{color:var(--spruce);font-style:italic;}
  @media (max-width:640px){.packgrid{columns:1;}.phrases{font-size:13px;}}

  @media (max-width:640px){
    header{padding:44px 24px 30px;}
    .lede{font-size:16.5px;}
    .stats{gap:18px 24px;padding-top:18px;}
    .stat .n{font-size:21px;}
    .ribbon{flex-wrap:wrap;}
    .ribbon .leg{flex:1 1 46%;min-width:46%;}
  }
  @media print{
    body{background:#fff;}
    header{margin:0;padding:30px 0 24px;}
    .wrap{padding:0 0 20px;}
    .contour{opacity:.08;}
    .day,.cross,.tier{break-inside:avoid;} dialog,.packadd,.hint{display:none;}
    .sec{margin-top:34px;}
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

  <header>
    <div class="contour" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 880 360" preserveAspectRatio="none" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4">
        <path d="M-40 250 C 120 210 200 270 320 230 S 560 170 700 215 920 200 980 175"/>
        <path d="M-40 290 C 130 250 210 312 330 268 S 580 205 720 252 930 236 1000 210"/>
        <path d="M-40 210 C 110 175 195 228 300 192 S 540 138 680 178 900 165 970 142"/>
        <path d="M-40 170 C 100 142 185 188 290 156 S 520 110 660 144 880 132 950 112"/>
        <path d="M-40 332 C 140 292 220 352 345 305 S 600 240 740 290 950 274 1020 248"/>
        <path d="M120 132 C 180 96 240 150 320 120 S 470 78 560 110" stroke-dasharray="2 7"/>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <p class="eyebrow">Evan &amp; Erin · Anti-clockwise · Summer 2027</p>
    <h1>Tour du<br>Mont Blanc<span class="small">June 28 – July 9, 2027</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">A full loop of the massif on foot, through France, Italy, and Switzerland. <em>Two sisters, ten walking stages, two rest days, three borders on foot.</em></p>

    <div class="stats">
      <div class="stat"><div class="n">~102</div><div class="l">Miles</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="n">~34,000</div><div class="l">Feet climbed</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="n">10</div><div class="l">Hiking days</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="n">2</div><div class="l">Rest days</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="n">3</div><div class="l">Countries</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="n" id="countdown">·</div><div class="l">Days to go</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="ribbon">
      <span class="leg fr">FR <small>Houches→Seigne</small></span>
      <span class="leg it">IT <small>Val Veny→Ferret</small></span>
      <span class="leg ch">CH <small>Ferret→Balme</small></span>
      <span class="leg fr2">FR <small>finish</small></span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <p class="sec">The Route, Day by Day</p>
  <div class="sec-rule"></div>
  <p class="hint">Tap any underlined lodging for details, a postcard, and its photos &amp; map.</p>

  <div class="trail">

    <div class="day">
      <div class="spinecol"><div class="node">01</div></div>
      <div class="content">
        <div class="date">Mon · June 28</div>
        <p class="route">Les Houches → Les Contamines <span class="via">via Col de Tricot</span></p>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="stay"><button class="lodge" data-lodge="gaisoleil">Chalet Hôtel Gai Soleil</button><span class="tag">B&amp;B</span></span>
          <span class="metrics"><span class="dist">~10.5 mi</span><span class="up">↑ 4,400 ft</span></span>
        </div>
        <p class="prox">In Les Contamines, on the valley trail · about 5 min off route</p>
        <p class="note">The harder, prettier opener under the Bionnassay glacier. Jacuzzi and sauna waiting at the end of the day.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="day">
      <div class="spinecol"><div class="node">02</div></div>
      <div class="content">
        <div class="date">Tue · June 29</div>
        <p class="route">Les Contamines → Les Chapieux <span class="via">via Col du Bonhomme</span></p>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="stay"><button class="lodge" data-lodge="nova">Auberge de la Nova</button><span class="tag">Gîte</span></span>
          <span class="metrics"><span class="dist">~11 mi</span><span class="up">↑ 4,750 ft</span></span>
        </div>
        <p class="prox">In the Les Chapieux hamlet · directly on the trail</p>
        <p class="note">A long climb over two cols into the quiet Beaufortain. Optional higher Col des Fours if the weather is clear.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="cross">
      <div class="spinecol"><div class="pin"></div></div>
      <div class="label">Enter Italy<small>Col de la Seigne · 8,255 ft</small></div>
    </div>

    <div class="day">
      <div class="spinecol"><div class="node">03</div></div>
      <div class="content">
        <div class="date">Wed · June 30</div>
        <p class="route">Les Chapieux → Rifugio Elisabetta <span class="via">via Col de la Seigne</span></p>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="stay"><button class="lodge" data-lodge="elisabetta">Rifugio Elisabetta</button><span class="tag">Refuge</span></span>
          <span class="metrics"><span class="dist">~9.5 mi</span><span class="up">↑ 3,300 ft</span></span>
        </div>
        <p class="prox">Directly on the trail, at the head of Val Veny</p>
        <p class="note">Glacier-side hut at the head of Val Veny. Books out fast, so reserve the day the platform opens.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="day">
      <div class="spinecol"><div class="node">04</div></div>
      <div class="content">
        <div class="date">Thu · July 1</div>
        <p class="route">Rifugio Elisabetta → Courmayeur <span class="via">via Mont Favre balcony</span></p>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="stay"><button class="lodge" data-lodge="coeur">Au Cœur Des Neiges</button><span class="tag">B&amp;B</span></span>
          <span class="metrics"><span class="dist">~11 mi</span><span class="up">↑ 2,300 ft</span></span>
        </div>
        <p class="prox">Dolonne side of Courmayeur, where the trail comes in · ~5–10 min to the center</p>
        <p class="note">Balcony views the whole way down, then a real town: shower, laundry, Italian dinner.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="day restday">
      <div class="spinecol"><div class="node rest">REST</div></div>
      <div class="content">
        <div class="date">Fri · July 2</div>
        <p class="route">Rest day in Courmayeur</p>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="stay"><button class="lodge" data-lodge="coeur">Au Cœur Des Neiges</button> · heated pool &amp; spa</span>
        </div>
        <p class="note">Placed right after the toughest opening stretch. Book both nights as one reservation.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="day">
      <div class="spinecol"><div class="node">06</div></div>
      <div class="content">
        <div class="date">Sat · July 3</div>
        <p class="route">Courmayeur → Rifugio Bonatti <span class="via">via Mont de la Saxe</span></p>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="stay"><button class="lodge" data-lodge="bonatti">Rifugio Bonatti</button><span class="tag">Refuge</span></span>
          <span class="metrics"><span class="dist">~8 mi</span><span class="up">↑ 4,300 ft</span></span>
        </div>
        <p class="prox">Directly on the trail · the balcony path continues from its door</p>
        <p class="note">The best Grandes Jorasses views on the whole circuit. Short distance, big payoff. The other must-book hut.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="cross">
      <div class="spinecol"><div class="pin"></div></div>
      <div class="label">Enter Switzerland<small>Grand Col Ferret · 8,323 ft</small></div>
    </div>

    <div class="day">
      <div class="spinecol"><div class="node">07</div></div>
      <div class="content">
        <div class="date">Sun · July 4</div>
        <p class="route">Rifugio Bonatti → La Fouly <span class="via">via Grand Col Ferret</span></p>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="stay"><button class="lodge" data-lodge="lafouly">Gîte / hotel, La Fouly</button><span class="tag">Gîte</span></span>
          <span class="metrics"><span class="dist">~12 mi</span><span class="up">↑ 2,450 ft</span></span>
        </div>
        <p class="prox">In La Fouly village · on the trail</p>
        <p class="note">Cross the border at the col and drop into the Swiss Val Ferret. Longest day of the trip.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="day">
      <div class="spinecol"><div class="node">08</div></div>
      <div class="content">
        <div class="date">Mon · July 5</div>
        <p class="route">La Fouly → Champex-Lac</p>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="stay"><button class="lodge" data-lodge="lagrange">B&amp;B La Grange</button><span class="tag">B&amp;B</span></span>
          <span class="metrics"><span class="dist">~9.5 mi</span><span class="up">↑ 1,650 ft</span></span>
        </div>
        <p class="prox">Steps from the trail at the Arpette / Bovine junction · ~1 km (20 min) past the lake</p>
        <p class="note">Gentle valley walking to a little turquoise lake. La Grange is small and beloved, so email early.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="day restday">
      <div class="spinecol"><div class="node rest">REST</div></div>
      <div class="content">
        <div class="date">Tue · July 6</div>
        <p class="route">Rest day at Champex-Lac</p>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="stay"><button class="lodge" data-lodge="lagrange">B&amp;B La Grange</button> · lakeside</span>
        </div>
        <p class="note">Doubles as a weather buffer before tomorrow's high variant. Prettiest valley stop to linger in.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="day">
      <div class="spinecol"><div class="node">10</div></div>
      <div class="content">
        <div class="date">Wed · July 7</div>
        <p class="route">Champex-Lac → Trient <span class="via">via Fenêtre d'Arpette</span></p>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="stay"><button class="lodge" data-lodge="trient">Auberge du Mont-Blanc</button><span class="tag">Gîte</span></span>
          <span class="metrics"><span class="dist">~9.5 mi</span><span class="up">↑ 3,950 ft</span></span>
        </div>
        <p class="prox">In Trient village · on the trail</p>
        <p class="note">The trip's hardest variant: a boulder scramble to a notch facing the Trient glacier. Clear forecast only; otherwise take the Bovine route, same schedule.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="cross">
      <div class="spinecol"><div class="pin"></div></div>
      <div class="label">Enter France<small>Col de Balme · 7,188 ft</small></div>
    </div>

    <div class="day">
      <div class="spinecol"><div class="node">11</div></div>
      <div class="content">
        <div class="date">Thu · July 8</div>
        <p class="route">Trient → Tré-le-Champ <span class="via">via Col de Balme</span></p>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="stay"><button class="lodge" data-lodge="boerne">Auberge La Boerne</button><span class="tag">Gîte</span></span>
          <span class="metrics"><span class="dist">~8.5 mi</span><span class="up">↑ 3,100 ft</span></span>
        </div>
        <p class="prox">In Tré-le-Champ · directly on the trail, right where the ladders begin</p>
        <p class="note">Back into France at the col, with the Mont Blanc massif filling the view ahead the whole descent.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="day">
      <div class="spinecol"><div class="node">12</div></div>
      <div class="content">
        <div class="date">Fri · July 9</div>
        <p class="route">Tré-le-Champ → Les Houches <span class="via">via Lac Blanc &amp; Grand Balcon Sud</span></p>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="stay"><b>Finish</b> · Chamonix valley</span>
          <span class="metrics"><span class="dist">~12.5 mi</span><span class="up">↑ 4,400 ft</span></span>
        </div>
        <p class="note">The ladders, then Lac Blanc, then the grand balcony home. Longest, hardest day. A cable car down from La Flégère or Le Brévent shortens it if knees are done.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

