  <p class="sec">Booking Priority</p>
  <div class="sec-rule"></div>

  <div class="tier t1">
    <h3>Book first, the moment they open</h3>
    <p class="when">Central platform (Mon Tour du Mont Blanc) · opens ~mid-October 2026</p>
    <ul>
      <li><span>Rifugio Elisabetta</span><span class="d">Jun 30</span></li>
      <li><span>Rifugio Bonatti</span><span class="d">Jul 3</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="tier t2">
    <h3>Book direct as soon as dates are firm</h3>
    <p class="when">Own websites / email · don't wait for October</p>
    <ul>
      <li><span>Chalet Hôtel Gai Soleil · Les Contamines</span><span class="d">Jun 28</span></li>
      <li><span>Au Cœur Des Neiges · Courmayeur (2 nights)</span><span class="d">Jul 1 – 2</span></li>
      <li><span>B&amp;B La Grange · Champex-Lac (2 nights)</span><span class="d">Jul 5 – 6</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="tier t3">
    <h3>Book by end of November 2026</h3>
    <p class="when">Valley gîtes · comfortable, not competitive</p>
    <ul>
      <li><span>Auberge de la Nova · Les Chapieux</span><span class="d">Jun 29</span></li>
      <li><span>Gîte / hotel · La Fouly</span><span class="d">Jul 4</span></li>
      <li><span>Auberge du Mont-Blanc · Trient</span><span class="d">Jul 7</span></li>
      <li><span>Auberge La Boerne · Tré-le-Champ</span><span class="d">Jul 8</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p class="sec">Good to Know</p>
  <div class="sec-rule"></div>
  <div class="notes">
    <p><b>Cash</b>Carry roughly 50–70 € per night for refuges. There are no ATMs above the valley towns.</p>
    <p><b>Sleeping liner</b>A sleeping bag liner is required at refuges and most gîtes. Blankets and pillows are provided.</p>
    <p><b>Half board</b>Dinner and breakfast are standard at the huts and gîtes. Order a packed lunch the night before.</p>
    <p><b>Weather call</b>Fenêtre d'Arpette and Col des Fours both need clear conditions. Each has a safer standard alternative that keeps the schedule intact.</p>
    <p><b>The last day</b>If a gentler finish appeals more than the rest day, trade one rest day to sleep at the Lac Blanc refuge July 8 and split the long final stage.</p>
    <p><b>Direction</b>Anti-clockwise puts the sun behind you on the big Italian and Swiss balcony stages and saves the Chamonix-side finale for last.</p>
  </div>


